course: dictionary
lesson: 5751
title: Lovesick and the feelings in words
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some words tell you how a person feels inside, and lovesick is one of them. Read the clues around it: «She sighed at the window all day and wrote poems about him.» Sighing and writing poems about someone who may not even notice her show that she is lovesick.
explain: Lovesick means so much in love, often with someone who does not love you back, that you feel sad and dreamy and cannot think of anything else. Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: «She is lovesick» means she cannot stop thinking about him, and that makes sense.
explain: Read this example: «Someone who says they are lovesick means they feel so sad or excited about a person they like that they do not feel like eating; it is not a real illness.» Lovesick is a feeling, not a sickness you catch from germs. Stories often use it to make a character seem sweet or silly.
fact: Lovesick means so much in love that you feel sad, dreamy and cannot think of anything else.
fact: Often the person you are lovesick for does not love you back.
fact: Lovesick is not a real illness; it describes a feeling.
fact: Writers use lovesick to show that a character is miserable or silly because of love, and it is often funny.
exercise: «The lovesick knight wrote poem after poem about the princess, who never even looked his way.» What does lovesick mean here? | Ill with a cold and a fever | Very hungry after a long journey | Angry at the princess for being busy | *So much in love that he is sad and dreamy and thinks of nothing else
exercise: Dad jokes that Sam is lovesick because he sighs every time Maya walks past. What does lovesick suggest about Sam? | He is about to go on a long journey | He has a real fever and needs to rest | *He has feelings for Maya and cannot stop thinking about her | He is tired from running
exercise: Which word fits the gap? «After the party, Lily was ___ and could think of nothing but Tom.» | ancient | curt | famished | *lovesick
test: «Wearing his best jumper, Oscar was lovesick every time Kira smiled at someone else.» What does lovesick suggest? | He is wearing a jumper that is too big | *He feels sad and dreamy because of love | He is very hungry and wants lunch | He is singing loudly in the playground
test: Which statement about lovesick is true? | It means very happy and loud | *It describes a feeling caused by love | It is a kind of fruit | It is a real illness you catch from other people
exam: Mia says lovesick means you have a cold. Is she right? | Yes, lovesick means you have a cold | Yes, but only in winter | *No, lovesick is a feeling about love, not an illness | No, lovesick means very fast
